  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element\r\n\r\n> The ismap attribute, when used on an element that is a descendant of an a element with an href attribute, indicates by its presence that the element provides access to a server\\-side image map\\. This affects how events are handled on the corresponding a element\\.\r\n\r\nHowever, it doesn't quite make sense to append the coordinates to JavaScript source code. Should we ignore the ismap attribute in this case?\r\n\r\nChromium-side issue tracked as crbug.com/668583 ",
